   claim:
     "The two `deploy-system/` files an earlier lane kept back as unrepointable are now inside akasha, because the four modules they reached for are findable after all: three of the four are one module. They land loadable and uncalled, so the capability each holds is restored to the tree without being restored to the deploy path.",
   evidence:
-    "Landed 2026-09-03 at 774ef588d7. `two-deploy-system-files-kept-on-purpose-cannot-be-loaded` recorded that `running.ts` and `secret.ts` imported four files commit 7449c63fce had taken, and that the lane could not establish what each became. What each became, by symbol rather than by name:\n`../kubectl/kubectl.ts` giving `runKubectl`, `runKubectlOn` and `Ran` — `akasha/service-system/cluster-services/workload-deploying/workload-deploying.module.code.ts` at lines 51, 56 and 23.\n`../deploy/deploy.ts` giving `Plan` — the same module at line 39.\n`../service/service.ts` giving `ClusterService` — `akasha/service-system/cluster-services/cluster-service.page-type.ts:12`, whose `ResourceKind`, `Namespace` and `ResourceName` are each `string`.\n`../refusal/refusal.ts` giving `DeployRefused` — nothing. The class is six lines and now stands in `secret-placing` beside its only thrower.\n\nTHE ONE SHAPE CHANGE. The old `Plan` carried `service.namespace`; the akasha `Plan` carries `workload.namespace`, and `Workload` is `{ kind, name, namespace }` — the same three fields as the old `Running`, which is why `workload-census` states `export type Running = Workload` rather than declaring the interface again.\n\nHOW MUCH BODY MOVED. `git show --format='' -U0 774ef588d7` took both files as renames and prints six removed lines: three import lines, the `Running` interface, and the two `plan.service.namespace` spellings. Everything else is byte-identical through the same `formattedBody` pass, with a seeded control arm on each that differed.\n\nWHAT IS STILL OWED. `placeSecrets` should run before a plan is applied, and `akasha/command-system/commands/deploy/web-putting-up/deploy-web-putting-up.module.code.ts` is where the plan is applied. `unpaged` answers a question `nothing-in-akasha-names-a-workload-no-page-claims` records nobody asks. Neither is wired here, because the deploy command is another lane's, and wiring a secret placer into a deploy path is a change worth judging rather than landing mechanically.\n\nThe manifest gained `@akasha/git` and `@akasha/pages-system`, which `secret-placing` reaches. Neither module has an `exports` row, because nothing outside `@akasha/service-system` reaches either.",
+    "Landed 2026-09-03 at 774ef588d7. `two-deploy-system-files-kept-on-purpose-cannot-be-loaded` recorded that `running.ts` and `secret.ts` imported four files commit 7449c63fce had taken, and that the lane could not establish what each became. What each became, by symbol rather than by name:\n`../kubectl/kubectl.ts` giving `runKubectl`, `runKubectlOn` and `Ran` — `akasha/service-system/cluster-services/workload-deploying/workload-deploying.module.code.ts` at lines 51, 56 and 23.\n`../deploy/deploy.ts` giving `Plan` — the same module at line 39.\n`../service/service.ts` giving `ClusterService` — `akasha/service-system/cluster-services/cluster-service.page-type.ts:12`, whose `ResourceKind`, `Namespace` and `ResourceName` are each `string`.\n`../refusal/refusal.ts` giving `DeployRefused` — nothing. The class is six lines and now stands in `secret-placing` beside its only thrower.\n\nTHE ONE SHAPE CHANGE. The old `Plan` carried `service.namespace`; the akasha `Plan` carries `workload.namespace`, and `Workload` is `{ kind, name, namespace }` — the same three fields as the old `Running`, which is why `workload-census` states `export type Running = Workload` rather than declaring the interface again.\n\nHOW MUCH BODY MOVED. `git show --format='' -U0 774ef588d7` took both files as renames and prints six removed lines: three import lines, the `Running` interface, and the two `plan.service.namespace` spellings. Everything else is byte-identical through the same `formattedBody` pass, with a seeded control arm on each that differed.\n\nWHAT IS STILL OWED. `placeSecrets` should run before a plan is applied, and `akasha/command-system/commands/deploy/web-putting-up/deploy-web-putting-up.module.code.ts` is where the plan is applied. `unpaged` answers a question `nothing-in-akasha-names-a-workload-no-page-claims` records nobody asks. Neither is wired here, because the deploy command is another lane's, and wiring a secret placer into a deploy path is a change worth judging rather than landing mechanically.\n\nThe manifest gained `@akasha/git` and `@akasha/pages`, which `secret-placing` reaches. Neither module has an `exports` row, because nothing outside `@akasha/service-system` reaches either.",
 } as const satisfies Finding
